<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gooty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gooty is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anantapur">Anantapur</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, dominated by a hill fortress on a granite outcrop. The fort was one of the chain of strongholds that defended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>, and it was later held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> chief Murari Rao and then by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>, before coming under British control around 1800.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gooty.jpg" alt="Gooty" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imrx100 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gooty_Fort.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
